# Webflow site binding

This repository is permanently connected to one Webflow site. Do not ask which site to use.

## Canonical site

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Display name | Hombre Tribute |
| Site ID | `63af52b71504f950bae436f8` |
| Short name | `hombre-tribute` |
| Workspace ID | `6332cf104bdcdf01092d8c36` |
| Domains | `hombre-tribute.com`, `www.hombre-tribute.com` |

## Agent rules

1. Use Webflow MCP (`plugin-webflow-webflow`) for all Webflow operations.
2. Always pass site ID `63af52b71504f950bae436f8` (or read it from `webflow.json` at the repo root).
3. Do not call `list_sites` to choose a site unless the bound site ID fails or the user explicitly asks to switch sites.
4. If Webflow MCP reports `needsAuth`, call `mcp_auth` once, then continue with the bound site ID. Do not ask the user to pick a site after auth.
5. Never publish without an explicit user confirmation that includes the word publish intent.
